WEBVTT

00:00:04.820 --> 00:00:06.390
The meteor shower...

00:00:06.680 --> 00:00:08.070
What do you mean?

00:00:08.070 --> 00:00:11.600
We haven't been able to see a meteor shower ever since the Disc appeared.

00:00:11.880 --> 00:00:14.980
Even if we could, it's not for another couple of weeks.

00:00:14.980 --> 00:00:15.690
No, that's not it.

00:00:16.440 --> 00:00:19.440
Togawa-san's been waiting this entire time.

00:00:20.580 --> 00:00:21.820
Ever since that day, seven years ago.

00:00:26.380 --> 00:00:29.330
Guys, let's join the Hokubi Festival!

00:02:03.370 --> 00:02:04.710
Laters, Mizusaka.

00:02:04.710 --> 00:02:06.530
Yeah, see ya.

00:02:09.000 --> 00:02:11.520
Hey, you really gonna participate in the Hokubi Festival?

00:02:11.520 --> 00:02:13.680
Aren't you busy preparing for your transfer?

00:02:13.680 --> 00:02:14.930
Well yeah, but...

00:02:15.590 --> 00:02:18.790
I can't really help it.

00:02:21.090 --> 00:02:23.680
Shione, do you have any plans after this?

00:02:23.680 --> 00:02:25.270
Why are you asking?

00:02:25.270 --> 00:02:27.580
Huh? U-Um...

00:02:31.630 --> 00:02:34.660
Listen, I <i>really</i> need to talk to you about something.

00:02:40.470 --> 00:02:41.920
Do you think this will do?

00:02:44.380 --> 00:02:45.650
You really think so?

00:02:45.650 --> 00:02:47.110
Don't even worry about it!

00:02:47.110 --> 00:02:49.220
Just leave the rest to me!

00:02:57.210 --> 00:02:58.580
U-Um...

00:02:59.390 --> 00:03:01.230
Allowance acquired!

00:03:02.580 --> 00:03:04.080
That was way too quick.

00:03:04.080 --> 00:03:08.740
By the way, Shione, I wrote your name down as one of our group members.

00:03:09.360 --> 00:03:10.990
What? What do you mean "group"?

00:03:10.990 --> 00:03:13.950
For the Hokubi Festival, what else?

00:03:14.380 --> 00:03:15.870
W-Wait!

00:03:23.570 --> 00:03:25.580
It's not compulsory for the third years to participate.

00:03:25.580 --> 00:03:26.550
Hold on!

00:03:27.260 --> 00:03:28.210
Hey!

00:03:28.750 --> 00:03:29.750
All righty!

00:03:29.750 --> 00:03:31.550
Seeing as we're all here, off we go!

00:03:31.940 --> 00:03:33.070
I said, I'm—

00:03:33.070 --> 00:03:36.350
Sorry, Togawa. You know how she gets, yeah?

00:03:39.410 --> 00:03:41.480
So where are we going?

00:03:42.330 --> 00:03:43.850
Shopping!

00:03:59.430 --> 00:04:01.250
What's that for?

00:04:02.620 --> 00:04:04.370
To stick on the fridge, what else?

00:04:05.290 --> 00:04:08.620
You dragged me here without a word. What do you even need me for?

00:04:08.620 --> 00:04:10.910
Yeah, I know what you mean.

00:04:10.910 --> 00:04:13.100
Hey! This was your sister's idea!

00:04:13.100 --> 00:04:14.560
It wasn't Yuzuki.

00:04:14.560 --> 00:04:15.840
Komiya was the one who wanted to.

00:04:15.840 --> 00:04:16.800
Huh?

00:04:17.580 --> 00:04:18.480
Nonoka?

00:04:19.100 --> 00:04:20.280
Why?

00:04:20.280 --> 00:04:21.520
How should I know?

00:04:23.010 --> 00:04:25.190
I figured you might have some idea.

00:04:26.720 --> 00:04:27.510
And why's that?

00:04:28.080 --> 00:04:31.160
You guys used to be tight, didn't you?

00:04:31.160 --> 00:04:32.660
You have a fight or something?

00:04:32.660 --> 00:04:33.700
That's none of your business.

00:04:34.700 --> 00:04:37.370
I used to think like that too.

00:04:39.270 --> 00:04:43.320
But sometimes second chances come from where we least expect them to, you know?

00:04:46.610 --> 00:04:48.100
Like you have any idea.

00:04:49.440 --> 00:04:53.220
How do you expect me to look for things when I don't even know what we're making?

00:04:53.220 --> 00:04:54.120
Oh, right.

00:04:54.970 --> 00:04:57.870
Komiya looked up what we needed herself.

00:05:57.310 --> 00:05:59.730
I'm back, Noel!

00:05:59.730 --> 00:06:00.320
Oh, I know!

00:06:02.210 --> 00:06:03.120
Here you go.

00:06:03.650 --> 00:06:05.300
You should come and visit our booth.

00:06:05.890 --> 00:06:07.500
"Hokubi Festival?"

00:06:08.780 --> 00:06:10.500
Hey, no fair, Koharu!

00:06:14.090 --> 00:06:17.030
Mine's the special golden ticket after all!

00:06:17.030 --> 00:06:17.880
Take mine, too.

00:06:20.000 --> 00:06:22.640
You can give them to your family or friends.

00:06:23.050 --> 00:06:24.380
Nonoka, look!

00:06:29.430 --> 00:06:30.770
I missed out.

00:06:31.500 --> 00:06:33.090
There's so many!

00:06:33.850 --> 00:06:36.150
But Noel can't go.

00:06:38.270 --> 00:06:39.150
Why not?

00:06:40.080 --> 00:06:45.290
Noel's the Disc, so if she's far away, bad things will happen.

00:06:45.820 --> 00:06:47.540
"Bad things?"

00:06:49.070 --> 00:06:50.230
Nonoka!

00:06:50.230 --> 00:06:52.690
Did you watch the meteor shower with Shione?

00:06:52.690 --> 00:06:53.920
No...

00:06:55.050 --> 00:06:58.800
But I'm sure we will, one day.

00:06:59.280 --> 00:07:00.490
Really?!

00:07:02.620 --> 00:07:04.970
Will Shione be happy like everyone else?

00:07:05.600 --> 00:07:07.480
It's all thanks to your message, Noel.

00:07:09.030 --> 00:07:09.870
Oh yeah!

00:07:09.870 --> 00:07:14.920
I stocked up the fridge today,
so I'll cook you anything you want, Noel!

00:07:14.920 --> 00:07:16.860
Really? Can you make omelet rice?!

00:07:17.140 --> 00:07:17.870
Of course!

00:07:17.870 --> 00:07:19.950
I'm gonna decorate it with ketchup!

00:07:28.780 --> 00:07:29.680
It's done!

00:07:31.350 --> 00:07:33.070
It kinda looks a bit bland.

00:07:34.150 --> 00:07:35.380
That's where you're wrong, Souta.

00:07:36.280 --> 00:07:37.910
Regardless of how it looks,

00:07:37.910 --> 00:07:41.380
this prototype has had a ton of time and effort put into it!

00:07:41.750 --> 00:07:43.060
This thing's going to light up like that?
First off, take the lightbulb.

00:07:43.060 --> 00:07:44.020
We etched Kiriyako Town's dazzling, starry sky

00:07:44.020 --> 00:07:45.290
It will! ...I think.

00:07:45.290 --> 00:07:46.740
into the plastic covering the lightbulb!

00:07:46.740 --> 00:07:47.890
Let's give it a try!

00:07:50.530 --> 00:07:52.280
We should make the room darker.

00:07:53.630 --> 00:07:56.690
Maybe we can use that thing you made, Togawa.

00:07:59.720 --> 00:08:00.940
Yup, this will work great!

00:08:01.480 --> 00:08:03.650
I helped in making it, so I wanna see too!

00:08:03.650 --> 00:08:06.950
Yuzuki, we all helped out too, you know.

00:08:08.550 --> 00:08:09.780
Right, Shione?

00:08:10.380 --> 00:08:11.960
I didn't really...

00:08:12.640 --> 00:08:14.330
We can take turns looking if it turns out well!

00:08:15.030 --> 00:08:15.930
Like I said, I didn't—

00:08:15.930 --> 00:08:17.430
Hey, get a move on!

00:08:17.430 --> 00:08:18.850
Okay.

00:08:22.490 --> 00:08:24.840
Okay, I'm turning it on.

00:08:28.140 --> 00:08:28.710
Eh?

00:08:28.710 --> 00:08:29.940
Is something wrong?

00:08:29.940 --> 00:08:31.730
There's not enough light.

00:08:32.160 --> 00:08:34.100
Try turning up the power.

00:08:34.410 --> 00:08:36.520
Well, maybe we shouldn't—

00:08:36.520 --> 00:08:37.980
Give it here for a sec.

00:08:37.980 --> 00:08:40.190
Ah, Yuzuki! Don't!

00:08:40.190 --> 00:08:41.230
Just a bit! Give it here!

00:08:41.710 --> 00:08:43.610
What's going on in there?

00:08:43.960 --> 00:08:46.190
Crank it to the max!

00:08:52.690 --> 00:08:54.410
Water! Hurry!

00:08:54.410 --> 00:08:55.210
O-Okay!

00:08:55.540 --> 00:08:57.290
No! Cut the power first!

00:09:01.270 --> 00:09:02.790
That was close...

00:09:02.790 --> 00:09:04.030
I'm back!

00:09:04.030 --> 00:09:05.340
Koharu, no!

00:09:10.350 --> 00:09:11.810
I'm so sorry.

00:09:12.520 --> 00:09:14.920
No, it's my fault it didn't work properly.

00:09:16.660 --> 00:09:17.810
Oh well.

00:09:18.470 --> 00:09:20.940
Hang on, do you always carry a pack of these with you?

00:09:21.240 --> 00:09:23.690
I was thinking we could share them together today.

00:09:28.230 --> 00:09:29.570
They're so good!

00:09:38.670 --> 00:09:39.830
Let's have them together.

00:09:43.250 --> 00:09:45.470
C'mon over!

00:10:00.090 --> 00:10:02.860
This brings back so many memories, doesn't it?

00:10:04.050 --> 00:10:05.590
You mean from the observatory?

00:10:05.590 --> 00:10:06.590
Right!

00:10:06.590 --> 00:10:08.860
Nonoka wanted to call the Disc,

00:10:09.170 --> 00:10:11.740
so we all got together like we are now.

00:10:11.740 --> 00:10:16.250
We all talked about how we'd do it,
and we even tried a few plans!

00:10:16.250 --> 00:10:19.300
It seems so silly now that I think back to it.

00:10:19.300 --> 00:10:20.960
That was a lot of fun...

00:10:20.960 --> 00:10:23.410
But the Disc really did appear!

00:10:29.000 --> 00:10:32.260
Was that really our doing?

00:10:32.570 --> 00:10:33.390
Huh?

00:10:35.480 --> 00:10:36.420
Togawa-san?

00:10:40.550 --> 00:10:41.900
Togawa-san?!

00:10:44.270 --> 00:10:45.690
Togawa-san!

00:10:48.710 --> 00:10:49.950
I'll be going now!

00:11:10.770 --> 00:11:11.930
Your friends?

00:11:13.370 --> 00:11:13.880
Yup.

00:11:14.500 --> 00:11:17.690
But we're in different schools, so I can only see them here.

00:11:18.170 --> 00:11:22.210
Yuzuki and Souta are twins,
but they don't look much like each other.

00:11:22.210 --> 00:11:24.350
They get along really well though!

00:11:24.350 --> 00:11:25.070
Right!

00:11:25.460 --> 00:11:28.170
Koharu is really, really nice!

00:11:28.170 --> 00:11:29.190
Right, right!

00:11:29.190 --> 00:11:30.860
And then there's Shione!

00:11:30.860 --> 00:11:33.580
Shione's friends with Mom, too!

00:11:35.730 --> 00:11:37.540
We're all gonna watch the stars together!

00:11:37.540 --> 00:11:38.670
The stars?

00:11:38.670 --> 00:11:39.280
Yup!

00:11:41.070 --> 00:11:47.070
We even promised to watch the meteor shower together...

00:11:48.540 --> 00:11:50.310
Meteor shower?

00:11:50.850 --> 00:11:52.720
Are you going to be here the whole time, Noel?

00:11:53.580 --> 00:11:54.880
Why?

00:11:54.880 --> 00:11:57.710
If you see Shione,
I want you to tell her something!

00:11:57.710 --> 00:12:00.560
"We might not get to see each other for a while, but I'll be back!"

00:12:01.250 --> 00:12:02.930
"I'll be back soon!"

00:12:03.740 --> 00:12:04.760
"So when I do..."

00:12:08.350 --> 00:12:11.620
"So when I do, let's watch the meteor shower together."

00:12:15.410 --> 00:12:17.370
Okay! Leave it to Noel!

00:12:19.840 --> 00:12:20.960
Thanks.

00:12:23.020 --> 00:12:26.590
Actually, I should really be telling her this myself.

00:12:27.730 --> 00:12:31.540
I don't want to say goodbye...

00:12:31.540 --> 00:12:34.050
Nonoka, are you hurt somewhere?

00:12:34.050 --> 00:12:35.640
What can Noel do to make you feel better?

00:12:36.250 --> 00:12:36.930
I know!

00:12:39.120 --> 00:12:40.840
I'll teach it to you too, Noel.

00:12:40.840 --> 00:12:41.350
Huh?

00:12:41.990 --> 00:12:43.400
This is Mom's song!

00:13:07.420 --> 00:13:08.750
Nonoka?

00:13:10.130 --> 00:13:11.170
Nonoka!

00:13:14.590 --> 00:13:15.390
Who are you?

00:13:16.530 --> 00:13:18.020
Are you Shione?

00:13:19.540 --> 00:13:20.270
Yeah.

00:13:22.950 --> 00:13:25.720
How do you know that song?

00:13:25.720 --> 00:13:26.480
Where's Nonoka?

00:13:27.700 --> 00:13:29.490
Nonoka went far away.

00:13:31.600 --> 00:13:32.960
What do you mean?

00:13:32.960 --> 00:13:38.540
But Nonoka said that she'd be back!

00:13:38.540 --> 00:13:42.710
She said she'd be back soon and that she wants to watch the meteor shower with you!

00:13:43.380 --> 00:13:44.340
Really?

00:13:44.340 --> 00:13:44.960
Yup!

00:13:46.400 --> 00:13:47.590
Thank goodness.

00:13:49.310 --> 00:13:50.090
Here.

00:13:52.360 --> 00:13:53.950
Thanks!

00:13:58.660 --> 00:13:59.600
What is it?

00:13:59.900 --> 00:14:02.660
Noel can't go though.

00:14:02.660 --> 00:14:03.620
Why not?

00:14:04.610 --> 00:14:06.270
Because Noel's the Disc.

00:14:06.270 --> 00:14:09.360
If she's too far away, bad things will happen.

00:23:32.200 --> 00:23:34.550
Next time, on Sora no Method:

00:23:34.550 --> 00:23:35.840
"The Meaning Behind Your Farewell."

00:23:35.840 --> 00:23:37.260
Look forward to it!
